# Real-user job in auto mode: a routine on-call fix (read the incidents MCP,
# edit the repo, add a test, run go vet and go test) should go through without
# a single permission prompt, because auto mode is meant to act rather than
# ask. EXPECT_PROMPTS lists every prompt IDLE had to answer, with the question
# it asked and its shot, so an over-asking auto mode fails with the reason.
@real
@home scratch
@size 140x45
@args --permission-mode auto
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/mcp-orders-svc
@setup mkdir -p {PROJ}/../bin && go -C {ROOT} build -o {PROJ}/../bin/incidents ./qa/fixtures/incident-mcp && printf '{"mcpServers":{"incidents":{"command":"%s"}}}' "{PROJ}/../bin/incidents" > {PROJ}/.mcp.json
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SHOT ready
EXPECT /auto mode/
SUBMIT_UNTIL /incidents\s+\d+ tools/ 60 /mcp
KEY esc
TURN orders-svc is paging... use the incidents MCP to figure out what's wrong, then fix it in this repo, add a regression test, and run go vet and go test
SHOT done
EXPECT_PROMPTS 0
RUN go vet ./... && go test ./...
RUN grep -RIl "page=3\|per_page=10\|page: *3" --include=*_test.go . | grep -v vendor
